digraph account_payable_process_91 {
	graph [rankdir=LR]
	START_NODE [label="" shape=circle width=0.3]
	subgraph CLUSTER_0 {
		"send to the vendor accounting department" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" [shape=box]
		"send to the vendor accounting department" -> "create a receiving report"
		"AND_SPLIT--3. Document validation_HEN9" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"create a receiving report" -> "AND_SPLIT--3. Document validation_HEN9"
		"report errors to relevant team member" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--3. Document validation_HEN9" -> "report errors to relevant team member"
		"double check a three-way match" [shape=box]
		"AND_SPLIT--3. Document validation_HEN9" -> "double check a three-way match"
		"confirm all documents have been amended" [shape=box]
		"report errors to relevant team member" -> "confirm all documents have been amended"
		"AND_JOIN--3. Document validation_HEN9" [label="+" fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"confirm all documents have been amended" -> "AND_JOIN--3. Document validation_HEN9"
		"double check a three-way match" -> "AND_JOIN--3. Document validation_HEN9"
		"check dates to avoid penalty charges" [shape=box]
		"AND_JOIN--3. Document validation_HEN9" -> "check dates to avoid penalty charges"
	}
	START_NODE -> "send to the vendor accounting department"
	END_NODE [label="" shape=doublecircle width=0.2]
	"check dates to avoid penalty charges" -> END_NODE
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following description is about the account payable process. It begins when you send to the vendor accounting department. 
When sending to the vendor accounting department is completed, creating a receiving report needs to be done. 
After creating a receiving report, the process is split into 2 parallel branches: reporting errors to relevant team member and doubling check a three-way match. 
Once reporting errors to relevant team member occurs, you need to confirm all documents have been amended.
Once all pre-tasks are executed, then you need to check dates to avoid penalty charges.
The process is now completed. 
"
}
